I'm guessing that the margin is there for maps which have a building
in the middle but which you can walk around. I think the solution
would be to change sp_lev.c to look from top to bottom of the margin
and check whether (IS_STWALL(lev[xstart][y].typ) && !may_dig(xstart,y)
&& !may_pass(xstart,y))  and if they all are, fill the margin with
unpassable and undiggable walls. Technically you might want to do a
search from the start position to check what's reachable by
digging/passwalling, and filling the rest with undiggable/unpassable
walls. This would also fix the sokoban Xorn-outside-the-level thing
that was mentioned lately.

Another possibility would be to add separate filling options for each
margin to the level editor, including undiggable/passwall flags. that
way the right of the ranger level would be open, but the left would be
trees.

While checking up on this I noticed that the left wall in the ranger
level is passable. Is this intentional? It'd be very bad to turn back
to normal form on the left side with no means of polymorphing back
into a Xorn, as the level is no teleport.

